      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to recognize that the least common multiple (LCM) of two numbers is the product of the numbers divided by their greatest common divisor (GCD). Given that the LCM of the two numbers is 36 and the GCD is 6, we can use these pieces of information to find the product of the two numbers.\n\nThe formula we will use is:\n\\[ \\text{LCM}(a, b) = \\frac{a \\times b}{\\text{GCD}(a, b)} \\]\n\nGiven that:\n\\[ \\text{LCM}(a, b) = 36 \\]\n\\[ \\text{GCD}(a, b) = 6 \\]\n\nWe can rearrange the formula to solve for the product \\(a \\times b\\):\n\\[ a \\times b = \\text{LCM}(a, b) \\times \\text{GCD}(a, b) \\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\\[ a \\times b = 36 \\times 6 = 216 \\]\n\nLet's use Python code to verify this calculation.\n```python\n# Given values\nlcm_ab = 36\ngcd_ab = 6\n\n# Calculate the product of the two numbers\nproduct_ab = lcm_ab * gcd_ab\nprint(product_ab)\n```\n```output\n216\n```\nThe product of the two numbers is \\(\\boxed{216}\\).",
